		(uuid "f7344ba3-908b-48aa-ac0e-49feba0f167b")
	)
	(text "The I2C_SEL pin selects I2C or SPI\noperation. The Si5345/44/42 supports\ncommunication with a 3.3 or 1.8 V \nhost by setting the IO_VDD_SEL (0x0943[0])\nconfiguration bit. The SPI mode supports \n4-wire or 3-wire by setting the SPI_3WIRE \nconfiguration bit"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 36.576 177.292 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3c81ab75-5121-4666-99fc-8e670c23dbaf")
	)
	(text "There are some applications that require better close-in phase noise performance. For these applications, a crystal oscillator (XO), can\nbe used as the XA/XB source instead of a XTAL. Some customers also tend to prefer to use an XO instead of a crystal for its superior\nreliability and performance over temperature.\nCompared to an externally mounted XTAL, an XO will have less total frequency error when taking into account all factors. Using an XO\ninstead of a XTAL will:\n• Deliver better accuracy in holdover since the accuracy of an XO is far better than that of a XTAL\n• Produce output clocks with lower phase noise for offsets less than 5 kHz.\n• Deliver greater immunity to vibration and airflow effects. This may result in lower phase noise below ~50 Hz.\n• Deliver better temperature stability with the frequency changes of an XO being less than that of a XTAL. Because of this, a jitter\nattenuator device can have a lower bandwidth and still filter out these oscillation frequency changes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 108.966 247.904 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.635 0.635)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "536a35d8-1a2d-48d8-838c-6689f4c61764")
	)
	(text "VDD=1V8!!!!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 148.59 76.962 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.254)
				(bold yes)
			)
		)
		(uuid "83a43185-4300-4b87-88fa-4f9e95df4e23")
	)
	(text "12.1.1 Si5345 Applications without a Crystal\nFor applications that do not use a crystal, leave X1 and X2 pins as \"no connect\". Do not tie to ground. There is no need for a crystal\nshield or the voids underneath the shield. The XA/XB connection should be treated as a high speed critical path that is ac-coupled and\nterminated at the end of the etch run. The layout should minimize the stray capacitance from the XA pin to the XB pin. Jitter is very\ncritical at the XAXB pins and therefore split termination and differential signaling should be used whenever possible.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.654 275.082 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "8f5512ce-9851-4200-a594-572e29ce8ea4")
	)
	(text "Unused"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 126.238 149.098 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c430db43-66cb-45ee-87e7-5fa51d86f05a")
	)
	(text "Control input (output enable/disable)\nLogic 1 or open on pad 1: Oscillator output\nLogic 0 on pad 1 : Disable output to high impedance"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 135.89 235.712 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ef8b04e0-6935-4f0a-9054-11c126c4be99")
	)
